From b89bd113d57448ec52e67e025df057868a6e107a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:50:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mcp): pick faces, edge chains and loops for an
 operation's area

Four MCP tools so an agent can choose what an operation machines:

- list_features: a model's planar faces (each boundary loop with the
  tangent edge chains that run it), edge chains, welded smooth faces
  and corner vertices, under their stable geometry-hash ids, written
  as "<kind>:0x<hex>" strings (a JSON number cannot carry a 64-bit
  hash exactly through every client).
- set_operation_geometry: the op's source becomes the picked features
  through SetOperationGeometry - one undo step, so undo restores the
  previous source. A loop is picked by the chains list_features names
  for it.
- get_operation_geometry: source, picks, area controls and the
  selection notes.
- set_operation_area: the area controls through
  EditOperationParams::with_area, one undo step.

Refusals are tool errors: malformed or unknown ids, a non-model, an
empty pick list, and a feature kind the op cannot take (a vertex for a
kind whose picks author its region, anything but a chain for
Multi-Axis Contour - generation's own refusals, said at the pick;
selection_drives_region becomes pub(crate) for it). Everything else is
the commands' own doors.

The handlers live in new modules (mcp/features.rs, pick.rs, area.rs);
tools.rs and mod.rs only gain the registration lines. Pinned by the new
mcp_pick suite: a pocket's floor loop picked off an imported STL,
generated, verified and posted inside the ring down to the floor, the
area set and undone, the pick undone back to the model source.

Fixes #180

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
